gainst 5@H.\n\n"],["pg",""],["lc","c8"],["pc","c8"],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["hs","ec"],["at","West's club lead is an obvious singleton which leaves South with 2 club losers. "],["pg",""],["ls","ec"],["ls","nc"],["ls","sc"],["hs","sd"],["hs","nd"],["hs","ed"],["at","South has a certain diamond loser as well and must hope that East is the only defender with a diamond guard. "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["ls","sd"],["hs","ec"],["at","In this case South may be able to arrange to squeeze East in the minors."],["pg",""],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["nt","South should start by winning the @CA in his hand as dummy's @CK will be needed as a dummy entry in order for a squeeze against East to be possible. "],["pg",""],["ls","ec"],["ls","ed"],["ls","sc"],["ls","nc"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","ca"],["pg",""],["hs","ec"],["hs","ed"],["hs","nd"],["hs","sd"],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["at","South has 3 losers - too many for a squeeze against East to be viable. South must try to lose at least 1 trick, but he cannot afford to lose the lead to East as a club return would destroy South's squeeze chances."],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","nd"],["ls","ec"],["ls","ed"],["ls","sd"],["ls","sc"],["hs","ns"],["hs","es"],["hs","sh"],["nt","Part of South's plan should be to eliminate East's spades so that a 2-loser squeeze against East will be possible. "],["pg",""],["ls","es"],["ls","sh"],["hs","ws"],["hs","sd"],["hs","sc"],["at","At the same time South should hope to reduce his loser count by discarding a minor suit loser on one of dummy's spades at a time when only West can win the trick. "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["ls","sc"],["ls","ws"],["ls","ns"],["hs","wh"],["hs","nh"],["hs","sh"],["hs","eh"],["nt","West is marked with 7 spades from the bidding and 1 club given the opening lead. West must have 2 diamonds for there to be a chance. South should therefore assume that West has 3 hearts. The dummy will have to be entered 3 times in hearts and this will only be possible when East's singleton heart is the