ill establish dummy's third diamond as a winner, while a club discard will allow South to play 2 rounds of that suit to set up a club winner in the South hand."],["pg",""],["up","7"],["hs","ws"],["hs","nc"],["ls","ec"],["ls","ed"],["nt","If West exits in spades instead of diamonds, a club is discarded from the dummy "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","nc"],["pc","sj"],["pc","c"],["hs","ed"],["hs","ec"],["at","and East is squeezed as before. "],["pg",""],["ls","ed"],["hs","sh"],["hs","sc"],["at","If East discards a club, South can either ruff and play on clubs or discard a club himself. "],["pg",""],["ls","ec"],["ls","sc"],["ls","sh"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","ws"],["hs","ws"],["hs","nc"],["at","Another club is pitched from dummy on the next spade (or on the last heart if West now plays a diamond instead of a spade) "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","nc"],["pc","st"],["pc","c"],["hs","ed"],["hs","ec"],["at","and East is caught in a more common 1-loser ^*Bcriss-cross squeeze^*N on this trick."],["",""]]}}